Build:

docker build -t my-updater-image .


Run while mounting Dockersocket:

docker run --rm -it \
  -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock \
  my-updater-image

(By default, updater.py will pull and start nginx:latest. can change when working properly)


Specifying a Custom Image:
If you want the updater to pull and start a different image, set the IMAGE_NAME environment variable:

docker run --rm -it \
  -e IMAGE_NAME=my_custom_image:latest \
  -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock \
  my-updater-image

Another container can invoke this updater container simply by running the docker run command above with the appropriate IMAGE_NAME environment variable set.



